513
00:43:36,705 --> 00:43:39,145
you would've known a long time ago, right?

514
00:43:40,225 --> 00:43:42,465
What? How is this my fault now?

515
00:43:43,185 --> 00:43:46,425
Krit, I'm seriously asking.
Why does it have to be Mochi?

516
00:43:46,985 --> 00:43:49,305
If it had been someone else,
maybe it would've hurt less.

517
00:43:49,385 --> 00:43:51,625
You know Mochi and I were--

518
00:43:51,705 --> 00:43:53,265
Were what, bestie?

519
00:43:56,745 --> 00:43:57,745
No.

520
00:43:59,065 --> 00:44:00,345
Ex-besties, actually.

521
00:44:05,825 --> 00:44:07,745
So you're doing this to get back at me?

522
00:44:07,825 --> 00:44:09,145
If you're saying that,

523
00:44:09,225 --> 00:44:10,865
it means you knew all along.

524
00:44:10,945 --> 00:44:13,865
You knew you betrayed me when you broke
our rule about no dating within the group.

525
00:44:14,545 --> 00:44:16,145
I didn't break the rule.

526
00:44:16,225 --> 00:44:17,825
We made it in high school.

527
00:44:17,905 --> 00:44:19,945
Krit asked me out after we graduated.

528
00:44:20,025 --> 00:44:21,265
Enough, Rin.

529
00:44:21,945 --> 00:44:24,985
I only came here to clear this up. Okay?

530
00:44:26,025 --> 00:44:28,225
It's not okay.
Who the hell would be okay with this?

531
00:44:28,305 --> 00:44:29,185
Of course.

532
00:44:29,265 --> 00:44:31,905
You're the type who always has to win.
You can't stand losing, can you?

533
00:44:32,505 --> 00:44:35,105
-Me?
-Yes, you.

534
00:44:36,145 --> 00:44:39,265
Then how about this?

535
00:44:39,905 --> 00:44:43,785
This semester, let's compete. You and I.
We'll compete through activities.

536
00:44:43,865 --> 00:44:45,825
Whoever has more followers
by the end of the semester wins.

537
00:44:45,905 --> 00:44:47,945
What the hell? What does that
even have to do with anything?

538
00:44:48,025 --> 00:44:50,425
Why? Are you scared?

539
00:44:51,265 --> 00:44:54,225
Who's scared?
Follower count? That's nothing.

540
00:44:54,305 --> 00:44:56,745
Watch me, little Mochi.

541
00:44:56,825 --> 00:44:58,705
I'll show you who the real top dog is.

542
00:45:18,265 --> 00:45:19,705
<i>Thanks…</i>

543
00:45:23,025 --> 00:45:25,065
for pretending to be my boyfriend.

544
00:45:29,745 --> 00:45:33,305
Actually, I've told Rin many times,

545
00:45:33,385 --> 00:45:36,825
but he always had an excuse for himself.

546
00:45:38,065 --> 00:45:40,345
Why did you decide to do this?

547
00:45:47,265 --> 00:45:48,825
When I'm with Rin,

548
00:45:50,705 --> 00:45:52,105
I feel smaller.

549
00:45:54,545 --> 00:45:55,385
I just…

550
00:45:57,065 --> 00:45:58,705
wanted to get out of that feeling.

551
00:46:00,065 --> 00:46:02,665
So you chose to play the red flag
and take all the blame?

552
00:46:03,305 --> 00:46:07,505
The person who breaks up first
always looks worse anyway, right?

553
00:46:10,145 --> 00:46:12,665
This way, Rin can meet someone better.

554
00:46:57,745 --> 00:46:58,825
Hey, Khobfa!

555
00:47:02,025 --> 00:47:02,865
I'm sorry.

556
00:47:06,345 --> 00:47:07,785
You almost got unlucky again.

557
00:47:08,785 --> 00:47:09,945
Thanks.

558
00:47:13,105 --> 00:47:13,945
Wait.

559
00:47:14,825 --> 00:47:16,985
Why do you have this pen?

560
00:47:18,025 --> 00:47:19,105
This pen?

561
00:47:20,065 --> 00:47:21,145
Well, it's mine.

562
00:47:26,425 --> 00:47:27,585
That's it.

563
00:47:40,625 --> 00:47:42,345
So this pen isn't yours?

564
00:47:45,305 --> 00:47:47,425
No. It's Khobfa's.

565
00:47:47,505 --> 00:47:49,305
I borrowed it and forgot to return it.

566
00:47:52,785 --> 00:47:53,865
All good now, right?

567
00:47:53,945 --> 00:47:55,225
Give it back.

568
00:48:09,785 --> 00:48:10,865
Oh, I'm sorry!

569
00:48:14,905 --> 00:48:15,745
Damn it.

570
00:48:16,425 --> 00:48:17,545
Shit!

571
00:48:24,825 --> 00:48:26,945
Am I really the mystic heir?

572
00:48:28,225 --> 00:48:29,585
If this spellbook is real,

573
00:48:29,665 --> 00:48:31,625
then there has to be a way to undo it.

574
00:48:35,185 --> 00:48:38,065
"If the curse is not broken
before the cursed person's birthday,

575
00:48:38,145 --> 00:48:40,065
that person will meet their end."

576
00:48:41,225 --> 00:48:42,385
I'm screwed!

577
00:48:50,265 --> 00:48:52,545
<i>Give me Khobfa's contact details.</i>

578
00:48:57,705 --> 00:48:59,905
<i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>cannot be reached at the moment.</i>

579
00:48:59,985 --> 00:49:02,225
Hey. Someone's hurt?

580
00:49:02,305 --> 00:49:03,865
Who's hurt?

581
00:49:09,425 --> 00:49:10,945
-Go check. Quick.
-Khobfa.

582
00:49:11,025 --> 00:49:11,865
Hurry up.

583
00:49:13,665 --> 00:49:14,665
Huh?

584
00:49:14,745 --> 00:49:18,225
-Hey, who's hurt?
-Is he hurt?

585
00:49:18,305 --> 00:49:20,585
-Is he okay?
-I bet this is serious.

586
00:49:22,945 --> 00:49:25,065
-Hey, listen up!
-Watch out!

587
00:49:26,145 --> 00:49:28,985
Rin!

588
00:49:42,745 --> 00:49:43,705
Are you okay?

589
00:49:47,145 --> 00:49:48,305
You're still alive.

590
00:50:16,105 --> 00:50:17,945
<i>What if I accidentally</i>
<i>used a curse from the spellbook</i>

591
00:50:18,025 --> 00:50:19,785
<i>to bring someone bad luck,</i>
<i>but I don't know how to undo it?</i>

592
00:50:19,865 --> 00:50:21,105
<i>What should I do, Mom?</i>

593
00:50:21,185 --> 00:50:23,625
<i>I believe everything has a way out.</i>

594
00:50:23,705 --> 00:50:26,665
<i>You just haven't found it yet, Rin.</i>

595
00:50:26,745 --> 00:50:28,185
Give it to me. I'll help you.

596
00:50:28,265 --> 00:50:29,785
<i>You're actually pretty cute.</i>

597
00:50:29,865 --> 00:50:31,625
But you complain a little too much.

598
00:50:31,705 --> 00:50:33,265
<i>Since when did you two get so close?</i>

599
00:50:33,345 --> 00:50:34,505
<i>Khobfa.</i>

600
00:50:35,105 --> 00:50:36,385
<i>Thanks.</i>

601
00:50:36,465 --> 00:50:38,105
<i>It's been a long time since anyone</i>

602
00:50:38,185 --> 00:50:40,265
<i>paid attention</i>
<i>to the little things about me.</i>

603
00:50:40,345 --> 00:50:42,385
Yes! Finally!

604
00:50:42,465 --> 00:50:44,305
I hope your bad luck is finally over.

